# Flutter Naming Conventions

- Use `snake_case` for feature folders (for example `user_profile`, `app_update`).
- Derive all names from one feature root and do not mix naming roots in one feature.
- Use singular PascalCase nouns for entities (for example `UserProfile`, `AppUpdateInfo`).
- Name models as `<Entity>NameModel` and repository contracts as `<Feature>Repository`.
- Name repository implementations as `<Feature>RepositoryImpl`.
- In `presentation/providers`, use:
  - `<feature>_repository_provider.dart` -> `<feature>RepositoryProvider` (camelCase)
  - `<feature>_state_provider.dart` -> `<feature>StateProvider` (camelCase)
- Prefer state classes ending in `State` and keep state files in `presentation/state/`.
- Keep feature widgets prefixed with the feature root (for example `app_update_sheet_*`).
